guamp: partial updates of the render server (bridge patch 0051 + PU row of the frame report)

fin53 (live-20261106-092610): the GuampMetal rows showed 9.6 passes, 100 draws and kpx=6263 a frame for a status bar change of 16 rows,
but kpx is width x height of each pass's colour attachment, not what the draws cover: the redraw of the whole frame was not shown. What
the log does show (row L, 331 s): 149006 shadow copies in (~12 a frame, each of the whole texture) and 58.95 G texels copied back
(~4.7 M a frame) for textures over buffers/surfaces that no linear image aliases. The bridge already copies back a loaded attachment only
inside its draws' scissors; this patch copies it in only there too (metal2vulkan ShadowUse::loads), when nothing else of the pass uses it,
and counts what is needed to tell whether Core Animation redraws only the damage: row PU (deltas between reports) = passes, colour 0
loaded/cleared, passes bounded by their draws' scissors with bound kpx / render-area kpx, shadow texels copied in / of whole images,
and passes into a >=1 Mpx surface (the framebuffer) by load action (load/clear/dontcare).
loadAction/storeAction/scissor/viewport were checked: translated 1:1 (render_target.rs load_op/store_op, render_state.rs scissors);
the render area is always the whole attachment, which on Turnip in sysmem (TU g0) costs nothing for Load/Store.
Applies after 0001-0046; adds bridge/patches/0051-guamp-partial-updates.patch (metal2vulkan 720ef1c + bridge 0001-0045).

